5,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,18,15,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,18,15,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,16,20,15,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,16,20,15,1124,611,220,17,284,220,22,20,198,257,1124,921,256,481,4695,11,220,22,20,374,537,74916,553,220,17,11,773,582,3271,311,279,1790,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,18,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,22,20,1124,611,220,18,284,220,17,20,198,257,1124,921,256,481,9295,11,220,17,20,374,537,74916,553,220,18,11,773,582,3271,311,279,1790,24632,10250,1372,11,892,374,220,20,624,257,1124,9640,257,220,17,20,1124,611,220,20,284,220,20,198,257,1124,921,257,1124,9640,257,220,20,1124,611,220,20,284,220,16,198,257,1124,21675,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,23526,504,279,74003,13,9258,1172,279,41171,13,3155,537,17024,279,6291,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe number 24 can be made by multiplying together four prime numbers: 2, 2, 2 and 3. How many primes must be multiplied to make 2400?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine how many prime numbers must be multiplied to make 2400, we start by finding the prime factorization of 2400.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of 2400:**\n   - First, we divide 2400 by the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n     \\[\n     2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n     \\]\n   - We continue dividing by 2:\n     \\[\n     1200 \\div 2 = 600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     600 \\div 2 = 300\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     300 \\div 2 = 150\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     150 \\div 2 = 75\n     \\]\n   - Now, 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n     \\[\n     75 \\div 3 = 25\n     \\]\n   - Next, 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n     \\[\n     25 \\div 5 = 5\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     5 \\div 5 = 1\n     \\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3f270e24f1f65c1e4786430c8348d2c75ec2380c6f4fe6839f0180455712524d"},"seconds":8.180415391921997,"seed":1022485419845042843,"stop":"eos","text":"Therefore, the prime factorization of 2400 is:\n\\[ 2400 = 2^5 \\times 3^1 \\times 5^2 \\]\n\n2. **Counting the Prime Factors:**\n   - We have five 2's, one 3, and two 5's in the prime factorization.\n   - Adding these together, we get:\n     \\[\n     5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n     \\]\n\nThus, the total number of prime numbers that must be multiplied to make 2400 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"Therefore, the prime factorization of 2400 is:\n\\[ 2400 = 2^5 \\times 3^1 \\times 5^2 \\]\n\n2. **Counting the Prime Factors:**\n   - We have five 2's, one 3, and two 5's in the prime factorization.\n   - Adding these together, we get:\n     \\[\n     5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n     \\]\n\nThus, the total number of prime numbers that must be multiplied to make 2400 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).","id":"prealgebra:753"}
